      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or are said to have committed, an offence against the Cremation Act 1929 (the penalty questions arise only then)
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest a doctor can be imprisoned for an offence against the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the doctor certifying the cause of death` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `imprisonment for` (`What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
